| A linked module keeps a string *field* of a particle it was sent, and reads
| it back on the next call. See `runtime_link_keeps_a_class_name.code` for
| why this can go wrong; this is the same fault reached through an ordinary
| field rather than `_class`.

link "native_modules/test_keeper.so" as m

emit NoteText { text = "eyJhbGciOiJFZERTQSJ9.a-value-worth-keeping" } to m get noted
assert noted ∈ Noted

emit RecallText to m get back
assert back ∈ Recalled
assert back.text = "eyJhbGciOiJFZERTQSJ9.a-value-worth-keeping"
